  "lead_raw_text": " The structure of SrZn₃ crystallizes in the orthorhombic space group Amm2 (No. 38), with a unit cell containing 16 atoms (Sr₄Zn₁₂) distributed over six independent Wyckoff orbits. Geometry-derived analysis identifies two Zn environments as close-packed-like with 12 geometric neighbors per Zn center (6 Zn, 6 Sr), while a second Zn environment shows 11 neighbors and a Zn environment 14 neighbors. Sr centers have 20 neighbors, and the periodic neighbor graph forms a single three-dimensional component. Validated polyhedron-sharing contacts include corner- and edge-sharing between 12-vertex Zn polyhedra, and corner- and face-sharing between 12-vertex and 14-vertex Zn polyhedra.\n<CRYSTAL_START>",
